WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.807
Here are three operators that are easy to overlook but very useful.

00:00:04.807 --> 00:00:11.827
Two asterisks mean exponentiation, so two to the power of three equals eight.

00:00:11.827 --> 00:00:15.957
Double forward slashes give whole-number division.

00:00:15.957 --> 00:00:22.787
One hundred twenty-five floor-divided by sixty gives two complete groups of sixty.

00:00:22.787 --> 00:00:29.508
The percent sign gives the remainder, so one hundred twenty-five modulo sixty gives five.

00:00:30.190 --> 00:00:33.387
Floor division and modulo often work together.

00:00:33.387 --> 00:00:42.627
For one hundred twenty-five minutes, floor division tells us there are two full hours and modulo tells us five minutes

00:00:42.627 --> 00:00:47.666
remain. Run the example and make sure the logic makes sense, not just the output.
